## What this predicate means

**A `has-part` B** — B is a structural part of A; A is the composite, B is contained.  The containment-down direction of the mereology relation.

Common shapes:
- A library has-part a chapter (sub-page)
- A plan has-part a stage
- A memorial has-part a section (when sections are reified as memorials)

